{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And behold, a ladder.</b> סולם (ladder) in gematria is סיני (Sinai), for he saw a model of what the Holy One, blessed be He, was destined to do — to give the Torah to Israel upon Mount Sinai." "<b>Set upon the earth, etc.</b> Corresponding to: 'at Sinai, burning with fire, unto the heart of heaven.'" "<b>And behold, angels of Elohim.</b> This is Moses and Aaron." "<b>And behold, YHWH stood over him.</b> This is as it says: 'וירד ה' על הר סיני.'" "<b>And He said: I am YHWH.</b> This is as it says: 'אנכי ה' אלהיך.' Another explanation: it was an actual ladder, and 'behold, angels of Elohim' — the Holy One, blessed be He, showed Jacob the prince of Egypt ascending (as written in the commentary of the Ramban z\"l). Another explanation: 'And behold, angels of Elohim ascending' — these are the angels who went to overturn Sodom, who appropriated honor to themselves, for they said 'כי משחיתים אנחנו,' and also they revealed the secrets of the Holy One, blessed be He; therefore they were banished from the presence of the Holy One, blessed be He, for 138 years, and now they ascended."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:15.601603037Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}